TITLE = 'Από την πρόβλεψη στην παρέμβαση'
OUTLINE = [
('Άνοιγμα', [
 (1,'','Από την πρόβλεψη στην παρέμβαση','Title slide, name and affiliation as on your decks.',''),
 (1,'','Το πλάνο της βραδιάς','Three parts with clock times: από την πρόβλεψη στην παρέμβαση · Εργαστήριο 2 και θέματα ηθικής · νέες κατευθύνσεις και εργασία. No footline.',''),
 (1,'','Πού βρισκόμαστε: δεδομένα → δείκτης → ανάλυση → δράση','The thread of the Week 1 roadmap with «δράση» lit, and the sentence Week 2 left open: «Ποια είναι η επόμενη καλύτερη ενέργεια; Για ποιον, από ποιον, πότε.» These words are the structure of the part.',''),
]),
('Η πρόβλεψη γίνεται απόφαση', [
 (1,'LAB1','Η οθόνη του Εργαστηρίου 1, την επόμενη ημέρα','The teacher screen they saw last week: 298 εγγεγραμμένοι, 192 επισημαίνονται (64%). Three people teach the course. What happens now?','Lab 1 case (simulated), this year\'s cohort'),
 (2,'LAB1','Το 70% σε πρόσωπα','The combined rule as four groups of people: 129 επισημάνθηκαν ορθά · 63 επισημάνθηκαν χωρίς λόγο · 26 δεν επισημάνθηκαν και δεν πέρασαν · 80 ορθά εκτός λίστας. The four cells are named once (ψευδώς θετικό, ψευδώς αρνητικό, ευστοχία/precision 67%, ανάκληση/recall 83%); no lecture on the confusion matrix, the cohort knows it.','Lab 1 case'),
 (2,'LAB1','Το κατώφλι είναι απόφαση, όχι ιδιότητα του μοντέλου','P(E→S) with the cut moved: 0,25 / 0,35 / 0,45 / 0,55 → επισημαίνονται 53 / 98 / 142 / 175 · χωρίς λόγο 8 / 25 / 54 / 73 · διαφεύγουν 110 / 82 / 67 / 53. From 0,25 to 0,55: 57 more students found, 65 more alerted for nothing.','Lab 1 case'),
 (1,'','Το κατώφλι προκύπτει από το κόστος των δύο σφαλμάτων','One line of decision theory for a CS cohort: επισήμανση όταν p > C(ψευδώς θετικό) / [C(ψευδώς θετικό) + C(ψευδώς αρνητικό)]. If a missed student costs five times an unnecessary contact, the cut is 1/6, not 0,5. So the real question is what each error costs, and to whom.','Textbook decision theory (no empirical claim)'),
]),
('Το ανθρώπινο κόστος', [
 (2,'POLL','Ερώτημα: ποιο σφάλμα βαρύνει περισσότερο;','The one timed question (60 s, Zoom poll). Context = the sentence from your old practical key: «οι ψευδώς θετικοί είναι αποδεκτοί: καλύτερα να προσφέρουμε επιπλέον υποστήριξη παρά να χάσουμε κάποιον». Συμφωνώ / Διαφωνώ / Εξαρτάται από την παρέμβαση. The next slides do not depend on the result.','Your E3 key, DS1'),
 (1,'LAB1','Ψευδώς αρνητικό: ο φοιτητής που δεν επισημάνθηκε','26 people. No support, and nobody audits the students who were not flagged, so the error stays invisible. One-line callback: in the 2019 Turku cohort the model found 35% of those who failed.','Lab 1 case · Veerasamy et al. (2022), already on Week 2'),
 (2,'LAB1','Ψευδώς θετικό: ο φοιτητής που επισημάνθηκε χωρίς λόγο','63 people. Four costs. The message itself: even well-made analytics feedback often provokes negative emotion, and here nothing offsets it. The adviser hour taken from someone who needed it: inefficient targeting is one reason dropout programmes show no effect. Alarm fatigue: the list stops being trusted (stated as a risk, not as a finding). Advice that steers the student (the EAB case, slide 21).','Lim et al. (2021), Assessment & Evaluation in Higher Education 46(3) · Eegdeman et al. (2023)'),
 (1,'','Το κόστος το ορίζει η παρέμβαση, όχι το μοντέλο','Three-row table: light action useful to anyone (message with resources) tolerates many false positives → low cut; scarce human action (meeting) → high cut; heavy action (compulsory step, change of track) → almost none. Answers the poll without depending on it.','Own reasoning (no empirical claim)'),
]),
('Περιορισμένη δυναμικότητα', [
 (1,'LAB1','192 επισημάνσεις, 60 διαθέσιμες συναντήσεις','Capacity turns the cut into a ranking. The 60 students with the lowest P(E→S): 51 truly at risk (85%), but they are one third of the 155 who will not pass.','Lab 1 case'),
 (1,'','Ευστοχία στη δυναμικότητα (precision at k)','The metric has to match the decision: accuracy and AUC describe the model, precision among the k we can actually see describes the service. Dutch vocational education: «invitation rules» that make the sensitivity/precision trade-off explicit under counselling capacity; inefficient targeting as one reason dropout programmes show no effect.','Eegdeman, Cornelisz, Meeter & van Klaveren (2023), Education Economics 31(3)'),
 (1,'SKIP','Ποιους δεν βλέπει η κατάταξη','67 students have no P(E→S) value and cannot be ranked at all; 39 of them will not pass. 39% of working students are in that group against 18% of the rest. The ranking inherits the measurement problem of Lab 1.','Lab 1 case'),
]),
('Δικαιοσύνη μεταξύ υποομάδων', [
 (2,'LAB1','Ίδιος κανόνας, άνισα σφάλματα','Among students who PASSED: flagged 90% of working students (26 of 29) against 32% of the others (37 of 114). Among those who did not pass: missed 3% against 21%. The rule over-alerts one group and under-detects the other. The variable «εργάζεται» was never in the rule.','Lab 1 case'),
 (1,'','Τρεις ορισμοί της δικαιοσύνης','Ίσα ποσοστά επισήμανσης (demographic parity) · ίσα ποσοστά σφαλμάτων (equalized odds) · ίση αξιοπιστία της επισήμανσης (predictive parity). Three cards, each with what it promises to the student.','Definitions as in Chouldechova (2017) · Baker & Hawn (2022), already on Week 1'),
 (2,'','Οι τρεις ορισμοί δεν ικανοποιούνται ταυτόχρονα','When the base rates of two groups differ, a score that is equally reliable in both cannot also have equal error rates. Two kinds of unfairness, then: in Lab 1 the base rates were almost equal (55% and 51% did not pass), so the gap came from the measurement and can be repaired; where base rates differ the gap cannot be removed, only chosen, and the choice is written down before deployment. Allowed exception to the 2020+ rule: it is the foundational result.','Chouldechova (2017), Big Data 5(2), 153-163'),
 (1,'','Σε πραγματικά δεδομένα: ποιους αδικεί η πρόβλεψη','Nationally representative US data (ELS:2002), usual features, several ML models: wrongly predicted to fail 19% of Black and 21% of Hispanic students against 12% of White and 6% of Asian students. The leading bias-mitigation techniques were «generally ineffective».','Gándara, Anahideh, Ison & Picchiarini (2024), AERA Open 10'),
 (1,'SKIP','Αρκεί να αφαιρεθεί το προστατευόμενο χαρακτηριστικό;','No. Large US university, residential and online students, models with and without four protected attributes (gender, under-represented minority, first generation, high financial need): leaving them out improved neither accuracy nor fairness; including them improved fairness marginally. In Lab 1 the rule never saw «εργάζεται» and still treated working students differently.','Yu, Lee & Kizilcec (2021), L@S \'21, 91-100'),
]),
('Όταν πήγε στραβά', [
 (2,'','Όταν ο αλγόριθμος έβαλε τους βαθμούς: Ofqual (2020)','Exams cancelled; a model standardised teacher grades from each school\'s history: 39,1% of about 700.000 teacher assessments in England lowered, 2,2% raised; disadvantaged students hit most, small classes favoured; withdrawn within days. Accurate on average, applied to individuals, no way to contest.','Ofqual figures as reported by The Guardian, ITV/PA (2020); Ofqual\'s own report to be opened at build'),
 (1,'','Όταν η φυλή έγινε «προγνωστικός παράγοντας»: EAB Navigate (2021)','Advising software in 500+ US universities; race in the model in at least four of seven documented cases; Black students labelled high risk at up to four times the rate of White peers; the score described risk «in this major», so the advice was a change of major. Texas A&M removed the variable afterwards.','Feathers (2021), The Markup'),
 (1,'','Τι κοινό έχουν οι δύο περιπτώσεις','Group pattern applied to a person · no route to contest or explain · errors never measured per subgroup before use. One line forward: these are the checks of Lab 2 and the obligations you will see in the legal framework of Part 2.','Own synthesis'),
]),
('Η παρέμβαση', [
 (1,'','Ανατομία μιας παρέμβασης','Five design choices, as a table: για ποιον (κατώφλι, δυναμικότητα) · τι (ενέργεια) · από ποιον (άνθρωπος ή αυτόματα) · πότε (εβδομάδα) · με ποια διατύπωση (μήνυμα). The human-in-the-loop question itself is kept for Part 2 (it is one of your seven).',''),
 (1,'','Τύποι παρεμβάσεων','Your own typology from the revision deck, in your wording: Αυτοματοποιημένες (emails υπενθύμισης, ειδοποιήσεις, εξατομικευμένα μηνύματα) · Εκπαιδευτικές (συνάντηση με σύμβουλο, επιπλέον υποστήριξη, tutoring) · Εκπαιδευτικού υλικού (προσαρμοσμένο περιεχόμενο, εναλλακτικοί πόροι).','Your «Μαθησιακή Αναλυτική: Επανάληψη», slide «Συστήματα Έγκαιρης Προειδοποίησης»'),
 (2,'LAB1','Δύο δρόμοι, δύο παρεμβάσεις','The promise of Lab 1 paid: χαμηλή δέσμευση → contact, barriers, goal for the next sheet; χαμηλή δεξιότητα → tutorial lab, content. A deployed European system makes the same split («at risk of failing» against «at risk of dropping out») and tested goal-setting messages on the current activity: 581 of 957 enrolled first-year online learners took part; dropout fell significantly.','Bañeres, Rodríguez-González, Guerrero-Roldán & Cortadas (2023), IJETHE 20(1), 3'),
 (2,'','Το ίδιο μήνυμα σε δύο διατυπώσεις','Left: «Το σύστημα σας κατατάσσει σε υψηλό κίνδυνο αποτυχίας». Right: what was observed, no label, one concrete next step, a named sender. Four rules of wording. Prepares the message the teams write in Lab 2.','Lim et al. (2021): students valued task focus and the sense that the instructor cares; emotions were often negative even towards good feedback. The rule «one concrete next step» is a design rule, not a finding.'),
]),
('Λειτουργεί;', [
 (1,'','Η ακριβής πρόβλεψη δεν αρκεί: πείραμα πεδίου στην Ολλανδία','Randomised field experiment at a large Dutch university: counsellors received each first-year student\'s risk. The system predicted accurately; dropout did not fall and performance did not improve. The authors: what is missing is actionable feedback and counselling practice.','Plak, Cornelisz, Meeter & van Klaveren (2022), Higher Education Quarterly 76(1)'),
 (2,'','Δέκα χρόνια έγκαιρης προειδοποίησης: Wisconsin DEWS','More than 200.000 students, AUC 0,80. Effect of the «high risk» label on on-time graduation: +4,8 percentage points, 95% interval from −2 to +11,6: zero cannot be excluded. School-level features target almost as well as individual scores. «The bottleneck is not identification but interventions.»','Perdomo, Britton, Hardt & Abebe (2023), arXiv:2304.06205'),
 (2,'','Τι λειτούργησε και τι όχι','Did not: encouragement e-mails to predicted dropouts in MITx MicroMasters (model found 80% of dropouts, e-mails opened, no effect); a dashboard with predicted pass chance plus weekly e-mail for 556 first-year Java students (more online activity, no effect on the exam). Did: changing the course content that caused the difficulty. Actions that remove the cause outperform messages about the risk.','Borrella, Caballero-Caballero & Ponce-Cueto (2022), Computers & Education 179 · Hellings & Haelermans (2022), Higher Education 83(1)'),
 (1,'','Πώς θα γνωρίζετε αν λειτούργησε η δική σας παρέμβαση','Flagged against not flagged is not a comparison (they differ by construction: the Course Signals error of Week 1). Three designs that are: a lottery among the flagged when capacity is short, comparison just above and below the cut (as in DEWS), phased roll-out. Also a reading rule for the assignment.','Own synthesis of the designs used by the studies above'),
]),
('Κλείσιμο', [
 (1,'','Να θυμάστε: τρία σημεία από το Μέρος 1','Το κατώφλι, η δυναμικότητα και το κριτήριο δικαιοσύνης είναι αποφάσεις που λαμβάνονται ρητά, πριν από τη χρήση του μοντέλου. · Κάθε σφάλμα αφορά πρόσωπο· το κόστος του το ορίζει η παρέμβαση που ακολουθεί. · Η ακριβής πρόβλεψη δεν είναι παρέμβαση: αποδίδουν οι ενέργειες που αντιμετωπίζουν την αιτία, και η απόδοσή τους ελέγχεται.',''),
 (3,'','Διάλειμμα','«Επιστρέφουμε σε 15′» with the 15:00 countdown. Next: Εργαστήριο 2, πραγματικά δεδομένα: κατώφλι, δικαιοσύνη, μήνυμα. Carries the 3 minutes of slack.',''),
]),
]

# Verdict on the old Week 3 material uploaded in this chat: (item, action, what I found, what happens to it)
